From: Jalal Hannan <jalal.hannan@midnight.foundation>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:09:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Regulated ZSwap CSL: authenticate gate route, hide
 binding, init protected type

Fixes three protocol defects found in review of 8285f69 and keeps the old
relation only as frozen rejection-test evidence.

1. Authenticated gate route (critical). The spend statement gains five public
   inputs [mode, gate_hi, gate_lo, ep_hi, ep_lo], constrained in-circuit to the
   witnessed gate/entry point the token-type derivation pins. Input::well_formed
   fills them from the input's public policy, so repointing policy.gate /
   policy.entry_point_hash or dropping policy on a guarded coin now fails
   verification. Closes the malicious-gate redirection (reproduced against
   8285f69; see ledger/tests/csl_regression.rs::attack_gate_substitution).

2. Hiding binding (high). The binding is now
   Poseidon(DOM[v2], nullifier, sender, token_type, rho) with fresh per-spend
   rho, a private witness of both the spend and gate proofs; it is never
   serialized or public. Removes the known-key recognition oracle and binds the
   spent token type across both proofs.

3. Protected-token configuration. A one-time admin `init` entry point sets the
   type (its transcript claims the cell is zero, so the ledger's replay makes it
   one-time); update_root writes the root only; authorize folds the gate's own
   type cell into the binding, so the gate authorizes only its own asset and a
   second asset at the same gate gets no authorization rather than sender-only.

The embedded spend verifier key is regenerated from the fixed relation; the v1
CSL relation is frozen in zswap_spend_csl_v1_historical (never dispatched) and
used by rejection tests. Wire layouts are byte-identical, so storable tags are
unchanged. Regression suite in ledger/tests/csl_regression.rs; reproduction
evidence captured separately.

